  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This paper presents a 3-qubit qGAN for approximate probability-distribution loading, trained on 20,000 samples from log-normal, triangular, and bimodal targets. On IBM Q Boeblingen, the authors train a 3-qubit, depth-1 qGAN for a truncated log-normal distribution over 200 epochs, then use the learned state for a classically simulated QAE option-pricing demo with 8 evaluation qubits: analytic payoff 1.0602, Monte Carlo on hardware 0.9740 ± 0.0848 (1024 samples), and QAE 1.1391 ± 0.0710 (256 samples).",
